  "body_html": "<h1>Mixed Strategy</h1>\n<p>For a finite or measurable strategy set $S_i$, a mixed strategy of player $i$ is a\nprobability measure on $S_i$. In the finite case the mixed strategy space is the\nsimplex\n$$\n  \\Delta(S_i).\n$$\nPure strategies are identified with Dirac measures. A mixed profile is an element\n$$\n  \\sigma=(\\sigma_i)_{i\\in I}\\in \\prod_{i\\in I}\\Delta(S_i).\n$$</p>\n<h2>References</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>[MFoGT, Section 1.3.5] Laraki, Renault, and Sorin, <em>Mathematical Foundations of Game Theory</em>, <code>references/MathFoundationsGameTheory.pdf</code>. Mixed extensions and pure strategies as Dirac masses.</li>\n<li>[MFoGT, Section 4.2] Laraki, Renault, and Sorin, <em>Mathematical Foundations of Game Theory</em>, <code>references/MathFoundationsGameTheory.pdf</code>. Mixed strategy profile in Delta(S_i).</li>\n</ul>",
